 "extrapolation_5min": "No 5-minute frames exist, so no 5-minute figure is measured. The hourly measurement above is the evidence: at 1 h spacing 84.5% of area-pairs keep their label and the gate (threshold chosen for <=0.0% missed label changes) skips 3.8% leave-one-camera-out. At shorter spacing fewer things change, so the skippable share can only be higher than the hourly figure; treat the hourly numbers as a lower bound. What is NOT known is the miss rate: the label changes that do occur within 5 minutes may be mostly small threshold crossings (half<->full), which are the hardest to see, so the per-change miss rate at the same threshold could be worse even though far fewer areas are stale (unmeasured). Measure it on real 5-minute frames before relying on it.",
 "notes": [
  "Labels are AI-teacher labels (84% of areas unanimous over 3 votes), not store truth; many tiny 'changes' are half/full borderline flips and compliance flips between similar-looking products, which no pixel gate can see.",
  "Thresholds in-sample use the same labels that judge them (optimistic); leave_one_camera_out is the honest figure.",
  "The per-area noise normalisation asked for was tried (ablation) and ranks label changes worse than a global scale.",
  "A skipped area keeps the previous answer; points_lost assumes that answer was perfect (best case), see scoring.py."
 ]
}